plugin-qualify (0.20.2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * tests: the steps and the daemon search the directories the fixtures are in
  * isolated-step: a refused add carries plugin-hostd's own reason
  * sync: the isolated and pool steps start plugin-hostd on the directories
    the sync scanned
  * release: build the DEBs beside the RPMs
  * Release 0.20.2
  * native: protocol.h from plugin-hostd-protocol where no -devel is installed
  * workflows: run in Open-Mixer while FreeMixer is restricted
  * release: a tag released by source-ref builds the arm packages too
  * lsan.supp: liblilv's world leak through a stripped library
  * workflows: run in Open-Mixer while FreeMixer is restricted
  * native, githooks: fetch the deps and the hook checker from Open-Mixer
  * release: a dispatch can release an existing tag
  * adapter admission: give a sampler its content before the notes
  * descriptors test: the fixture bundles are 21 since synth-attack and
    synth-delay joined
  * measure an instrument's latency to its first sample above silence, not
    its attack
  * A descriptor name writes a non-ASCII id one '_' per UTF-8 byte, as
    plugin-hostd reads it
  * 0.19.2: a CLAP file whose name holds a space is pinned, as one
    percent-encoded word
  * qualify-sync: a stray comma from the last change
  * check-installed: the sync gets a dummy JACK server for the LV2 fixture,
    or, where jackd is not installed, must name the missing server
  * tests: the sweep that admits an LV2 plugin under omx-clap-host has a JACK
    server, as a run with none now stops by name
  * 0.19.2: LV2 names with a space, no fake isolated debt, adapter run for
    failed probes, Pi cells at 96000, no JACK server stops the run
  * workflows: run in Open-Mixer while FreeMixer is restricted
  * ci: packaging runs on v* tags and workflow_dispatch only

 -- Pau Aliagas <linuxnow@gmail.com>  Tue, 10 Nov 2026 22:31:22 +0000
